{{JPExclusive}}
:''For the enemies encountered in the [[Castle & Dragon Collaboration Event]], see [[Dragon Rider (Enemy)]] or [[Flame Dragon Rider (Enemy)]].''
'''Dragon Rider''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked during the [[Castle & Dragon Collaboration Event]] by completing the stage [[Tradition]] with a [[Timed Score Reward|Timed Score]] of at least 4,500. It was added in [[Version 4.6 Update|Version 4.6]]. [[True Form]] also added in Version 4.6 doubles attack power.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 253
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Dragon Rider
|name2 = Horn Dragon Rider
|name3 = Flame Dragon Rider
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Horn Dragon Rider''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Flame Dragon Rider''' when obtained from the [[Road to Dragon Rider Evolution (Normal)|Road to Dragon Rider Evolution]] stage and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit has pretty much no use at all, regardless of where in the game you're at. In early game, its stats are very poor, its upgrade cost is too high to improve its usage and there are always better picks for its role such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] or [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]]. Later on, its role is non-existant. Units like [[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Macho Legs]] or [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] completely outclass it as a midranger, and Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] blows it out of the water.

At least it can help to get some [[User Rank]], if you don't have any cheaper or better unit to upgrade, that is.

{{Job|Classification = User Rank Dump}}

